  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The War Lament** (1 review): Reviewer likes this track, finding sadness in the female singer's voice that makes the song interesting [8]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Joe Gets An Assignment**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Joe Meets The Insects**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Insect Message Song**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Joe's Boss is Skeptical**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Joe Speaks On The Radio**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Pollution Song**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Joe Calls Lois**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Joe and Lois Are Reconciled**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd82-01-01.sbd.hanno.19808.sbeok.shnf** (recommended): soundboard; 23 songs; 42 min; rated 2.67/5 by 9 [1]. Said about its sound: Includes nice sound effects and musical interludes, among them a clip from 'Deep, Wide and Frequent'; Reviewer calls the recording high quality, and notes its rarity [3][5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer hears echoes of present-day public discourse in the radio play, and a reminder of humans' place in the ecosystem relative to bugs [6]\n- Reviewer likens the radio play to War of the Worlds, and says it is not a studio jam with banter [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd82-01-01.sbd.hanno.19808.sbeok.shnf**: source: Soundboard [1]. Also: Studio recording made by Mickey Hart, Barry Melton, Bill Graham and others; it is an unreleased radio play called 'The Bugs'; Circulating copy comes from a third-generation cassette, passed through Hanno Bunjes and Uli Teute [1]",
